{"name":"Sideshow","hex":"#e2c591","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sideshow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A minor attraction at a larger event such as a circus, fair or music festival.","An incidental spectacle that diverts attention from a larger concern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sideshow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sideshow","blocks":[{"text":"In North America, a sideshow is an extra, secondary production associated with a circus, carnival, fair, or other such attraction. They historically featured human oddity exhibits, preserved specimens, live animal acts, burlesque or strip shows, actually or ostensibly dangerous stunts, or stunts that appear painful like human blockhead."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sideshow","wikidata":"Q1534976"},{"title":"Sideshow (automobile exhibition)","blocks":[{"text":"A sideshow is an informal and often illegal demonstration of automotive stunts now often held in vacant lots and public intersections, originally seen in the East Bay region of the San Francisco Bay Area, United States. Sideshows first appeared in Oakland, California, in the 1980s as informal social gatherings of Bay Area youth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/SanJoseSideshow-Americancarculture-2021-7-11.webm/330px--SanJoseSideshow-Americancarculture-2021-7-11.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sideshow_(automobile_exhibition)","wikidata":"Q7508465"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Old_sideshow_ad%2C_firebreathing_man.JPG/500px-Old_sideshow_ad%2C_firebreathing_man.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Old_sideshow_ad%2C_firebreathing_man.JPG/500px-Old_sideshow_ad%2C_firebreathing_man.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Painting on sideshow truck, firebre